<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eóganachta</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Eóganacht, Eoganachta, Eoganacht</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Eóganachta were a group of related dynasties that ruled the Kingdom of Munster in early medieval Ireland, claiming descent from Éogan Mór. From about the 5th century their branches, such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eoganacht-chaisil">Eóganacht Chaisil</a> around Cashel and the Eóganacht Locha Léin in the west, shared the kingship of Munster. They lost it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-cais">Dál gCais</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brian-boru">Brian Boru</a> in the 10th century, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-maccarthy">MacCarthys</a> continued in Desmond.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eoganachta.jpg" alt="Eóganachta" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ramón · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rock_of_Cashel_-_15.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
